'''Vanqor''' was a rocky [[crystal]]line [[planet]] located in the [[Vanqor system]] of [[the galaxy]]'s [[Outer Rim Territories]] that was the [[homeworld]] of the [[gundark]] [[species]]. During the [[Clone Wars]], the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]] established a [[Vanqor listening station|listening post]] on this world.

==Description==
{{Quote|Charming place. Delightful fauna.|Obi-Wan Kenobi, on Vanqor|<ref name="Dark Disciple" />}}
Located in the [[Vanqor system]] in the far reaches of [[the galaxy]]'s [[Outer Rim Territories]],<ref name="Dooku Captured" /> Vanqor was a [[Temperature|temperate]],<ref name="VE" /> rocky,<ref name="Dark Disciple" /> and overcast [[planet]] with a surface marked by smoky [[crystal]]line formations.<ref name="Dooku Captured Episode Gallery" /> Swirling [[silica]]-dust [[Silica-dust storm|storms]]<ref name="VE" /> caused the world to have a [[Color|blue]]-gray hue when viewed from [[Realspace|space]].<ref name="Dark Disciple" /> Vanqor was located six [[parsec]]s away from the closest planet, [[Florrum]],<ref name="Dooku Captured" /> and was the [[homeworld]] of the [[gundark]]s, fierce, aggressive creatures known for their overwhelming strength who inhabited the planet's [[cave]]s.<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars">''[[Ultimate Star Wars]]''</ref> Also inhabiting some of Vanqor's caves were bio-luminescent organisms that lived on the cave walls.<ref name="DC">{{TCW|Dooku Captured}}</ref>

==History==
{{Quote|Our intel indicates that Count Dooku has placed a listening station on Vanqor.|Mace Windu|<ref name="Dark Disciple" />}}
[[File:Gundarks-R2CH.png|thumb|left|250px|A pair of gundarks prowling the surface of Vanqor]]
In the [[Standard year|year]] [[21 BBY]],<ref name="Galactic Atlas">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]''</ref> [[Jedi Master]] [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] and [[Jedi Knight|Knight]] [[Anakin Skywalker]] [[Skirmish at Vanqor|shot down]] [[Count]] [[Dooku]], leader of the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]], over Vanqor, forcing him to crash-land his [[Count Dooku's solar sailer|ship]] on the planet's surface. However, their [[Sheathipede-class transport shuttle|shuttle]] was also forced down during the ensuing battle. On Vanqor, Dooku abandoned his [[solar sailer]] and evaded the [[Jedi]] by hiding in a cave filled with gundarks; when they pursued him inside, Dooku used [[the Force]] to bring down stalactites, separating the Jedi and buried Skywalker, whose [[Skywalker lightsaber|lightsaber]] Dooku took before leaving the cave and collapsing its entrance. Outside, he was found by [[Hondo Ohnaka]] and his [[Ohnaka Gang|gang]] of [[pirate]]s, who agreed to take him to Florrum. Although the Jedi emerged unscathed, they were attacked by an angry gundark. While using the Force to build a barricade, the Jedi accidentally opened a fissure and noxious green [[gas]] began filling the cavern. As the pair tried to dig their way out of the collapsed opening, the gas began to overwhelm them and they collapsed just as the cavern entrance exploded from outside as Skywalker's [[Padawan]], [[Ahsoka Tano]], and her [[Clone trooper|clone]] forces blasted the cave open. After the pair exited the cavern, the clones eliminated the gundark by collapsing the entrance once more.<ref name="Dooku Captured" />

In [[21 BBY]],<ref name="Galactic Atlas" /> an [[Sabotage of the Endurance|attempt]] on Jedi Master [[Mace Windu]]'s life by [[Boba Fett]] resulted in the [[Venator-class Star Destroyer|''Venator''-class Star Destroyer]] ''[[Endurance]]'' crashing onto Vanqor.<ref name="Death Trap">{{TCW|Death Trap}}</ref> There, its commanding officer, [[Admiral]] [[Shoan Kilian|Kilian]], [[Clone Commander]] [[Ponds]], and a [[Clone navigation officer|navigation officer]] were taken hostage by Fett and his team of [[bounty hunter]]s, consisting of [[Aurra Sing]], [[Bossk'wassak'Cradossk|Bossk]], and [[Castas]]. While Windu and Skywalker were [[Mission to Vanqor|searching]] the wreckage for survivors, Fett made another attempt on the Jedi Master's life that left both Windu and Skywalker trapped under debris until they were rescued by Jedi Master [[Plo Koon]], Tano, and the [[104th Battalion]].<ref name="R2 Come Home">{{TCW|R2 Come Home}}</ref>

At some point, the [[Quarren]] [[pirate]] [[Kragan Gorr]] arrived on Vanqor and rescued the [[Mirialan]] [[Synara San]] off the streets of Vanqor.<ref name="The Triple Dark">{{Resistance|The Triple Dark}}</ref> San said that her and her father used to hunt on the planet.<ref name="The Doza Dilemma">{{Resistance|The Doza Dilemma}}</ref> She was grateful to him, but eventually considered her debt to Gorr to be paid by the time of the [[First Order-Resistance War]].<ref name="The Mutiny">{{Resistance|The Mutiny}}</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
Vanqor first appeared in ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[canon]] in "[[Dooku Captured]]," the eleventh episode of the canon animated series ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]''{{'}} [[The Clone Wars: Season One|first season]],<ref name="Dooku Captured" /> which originally aired on [[January 2]], [[2009]].<ref name="Episode Guide">{{SW|url=series/clone-wars/dooku-captured-episode-guide|text="Dooku Captured" Episode Guide &#124; The Clone Wars}}</ref> It was originally created for ''[[Jedi Quest: The Moment of Truth]]'', the seventh entry in the [[Star Wars: Jedi Quest|''Jedi Quest'']] series of younger reader novels written by [[Jude Watson]].<ref name="The Moment of Truth">''[[Jedi Quest: The Moment of Truth]]''</ref>

